{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you came in with chest pain after dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started around 4 PM. I went for my regular dialysis, but my access wasn’t working. They sent me to a vascular clinic, had a procedure, and then the chest pain started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Can you describe the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was pressure, right in the center, didn’t go anywhere. I also felt shaky, nauseous, and my heart was racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You took nitroglycerin in the ER and it helped?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, two under the tongue. The pain and palpitations went away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2117-08-24 23:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re checking your heart enzymes and did an EKG. Your blood pressure was high when you arrived, but it’s better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to aspirin—gives me hives. Is that going to be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. We gave you Plavix instead, which is similar but safe for you. We’re being cautious because your EKG showed some changes that could suggest heart strain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So it could be my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sure yet. Your troponin was slightly elevated but not high enough to confirm a heart attack. We’ll repeat it. We also need to check for other causes, like a clot in the lung."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A clot? Like a pulmonary embolism?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Given your history—being on dialysis, recent surgery—it’s a real possibility. We’re going to do a CT scan of your lungs with contrast to check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my dialysis access? It’s been weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2117-08-25 00:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed the thrill wasn’t strong, but we heard a good bruit. We ordered an ultrasound to check blood flow. We want to make sure the graft is working after your procedure yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2117-08-25 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your chest X-ray was clear, no pneumonia or fluid. The ultrasound of your arm showed some flow in the graft, but it’s limited. We may need a more detailed study."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2117-08-25 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s still blocked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2117-08-25 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not completely. There’s flow, but it’s not optimal. We’re consulting transplant surgery. For now, we’ll proceed with your dialysis as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We have results from your CT scan. There’s a small clot in the right lower part of your lung—a subsegmental pulmonary embolism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no. Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s small and not causing strain on your heart, so it’s not immediately life-threatening. But we need to treat it with blood thinners to prevent it from getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I be on that forever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Probably not. We’ll start with heparin injections and switch to Coumadin. You’ll likely need it for at least six months. We’ll reassess then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart? Is it okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2117-08-26 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re still evaluating. The chest pain could be from the clot, but we want to rule out heart ischemia. You’ll have a stress test tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2117-08-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had your dialysis this morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2117-08-27 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but during dialysis, my blood pressure dropped to 60. I had chest discomfort again—different from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2117-08-27 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. It resolved when your pressure came back up. That’s often due to low blood volume during dialysis, not necessarily a heart issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2117-08-27 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’m still worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2117-08-27 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Totally understandable. That’s why we’re doing a pharmacologic stress test today. It uses medication to simulate exercise and checks blood flow to your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2117-08-27 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The stress test is back. Good news: no signs of reduced blood flow to your heart. Your ejection fraction is normal—65%. No new heart damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2117-08-27 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So the chest pain wasn’t my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2117-08-27 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not from blocked arteries. The pain during dialysis was likely due to low pressure. But we also noticed you have some chest wall tenderness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2117-08-27 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, when I press here, it hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2117-08-27 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely musculoskeletal—maybe from positioning or strain. We can treat that with pain relief and it should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2117-08-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a fistulagram yesterday to check your dialysis access. It showed the graft is open, no clots. The stent they placed is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2117-08-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Then why is the flow low?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2117-08-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have a duplicated brachial artery, and both are small—about 3 mm. That limits blood flow into the graft. It’s anatomical, not a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2117-08-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So nothing can be done?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2117-08-28 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not surgically at this time. But your access is working well enough for dialysis. Transplant surgery will follow up to monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2117-08-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now therapeutic—above 2. We’re stopping the heparin injections and continuing only Coumadin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2117-08-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I won’t need shots anymore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2117-08-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. Just the Coumadin pill daily. You’ll need regular blood tests to monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2117-08-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2117-08-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing your usual medications. We added Plavix for heart protection and Nephrocaps for your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2117-08-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’ll go to extended care for rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2117-08-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be okay with the blood thinner?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2117-08-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, as long as you take it as prescribed and get your INR checked. Watch for unusual bruising or bleeding and report it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2117-08-30 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-ups?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2117-08-30 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have appointments with orthopedics for your knee and transplant surgery for your graft. Transportation will be arranged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2117-08-31 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go. Your chest pain was due to a small lung clot and some muscle soreness. Your heart is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2117-08-31 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2117-08-31 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on Coumadin 3 mg daily, Plavix, and Nephrocaps. Stop the heparin shots. Keep all your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2117-08-31 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And weigh myself daily, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2117-08-31 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2117-08-24 23:46:00",
    "admission_end": "2117-08-31 15:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with chest pain following a dialysis session and recent thrombectomy of her AV graft. Initial evaluation revealed a subsegmental pulmonary embolism on CT angiography, with no evidence of acute myocardial infarction despite a mildly elevated troponin and EKG changes. A pharmacologic stress test showed no ischemia, and her cardiac function was preserved with a normal ejection fraction. The chest pain was attributed to the pulmonary embolism and a separate component of musculoskeletal chest wall pain. Her dialysis access was evaluated with a fistulagram, which confirmed patency without thrombosis but identified a duplicated small-caliber brachial artery as the cause of low flow. She was anticoagulated with a heparin bridge to warfarin, which was continued at discharge. The patient remained stable, with resolution of symptoms, and was discharged to extended care with follow-up planned for anticoagulation management, transplant surgery, and orthopedics.",
    "problems": [
      "Pulmonary embolism",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Diabetes mellitus without complication",
      "Long-term insulin use",
      "Hyperlipidemia",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Asthma"
    ]
  }
}
